# Probe 36 (scripts/probe_apply_scatter_card_map.py): the acceptance probe for the scatter chart, the multi-row card and the map — every visual built by `bp apply` from a spec, nothing patched by hand.
# Seen (bridge captures, then a real refresh + Ctrl+S): all four predictions held. A1: every visual drew as its probe-34 candidate did — the multi-row card as 500 Total Amount, as two measures side by side, and as one row per country (FR 200, UK 300); the scatter minimal, with a Legend and Size (four sized, coloured bubbles with a legend), and with a drill-down category (four points, because Blueprint writes both drill levels active where the probe-34 candidate had the second false); and both maps as Bing bubbles per country, the Legend one split into Region segments. The maps drew without touching anything this time, so the Desktop security setting had stuck across a restart. A2: the save added `"active": true` to the X projection of all three scatter charts and changed nothing else — Blueprint leaves that flag out on purpose, because `active` marks a column's drill state and X takes a measure, so this confirms it is Desktop's to add. The two multi-row cards and the two maps were not rewritten at all. It also raised the three rewritten files' $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0, added its condition-less auto filterConfig and rewrote pages.json activePageName. Desktop did NOT flip the drill-down's second Category level to active false here (nobody drilled). A3: re-applying the same specs on the saved report changed nothing at all. A4: `bp check` reports no format findings; its 5 errors are the fixture's own hand-built page (theme palette/typography and two off-grid visuals). All content invented.

